One thing you should not overlook: the repository is MIT-licensed, but the repo also contains individual skills/components with their own licensing/attribution requirements. For example, one bundled PowerPoint skill has an Anthropic-specific license. So before redistributing a white-labeled build, audit every retained skill/resource, not just the top-level Hermes MIT license. 

Also, because Hermes is actively changing, I would pin a specific upstream commit/tag for your first enterprise release rather than building directly from main.